How the Track Page Fetches Data in Real-Time
The "magic" of the track page updating without a refresh happens through a Firestore Snapshot Listener. Here is the explanation of the flow:

The "Live Wire": When the user lands on the Track Page with their ID, your code creates a "Live Wire" (Listener) between the browser and that specific document in Firestore.

The Wait State: The page looks at the AI flag. Since the flag is 0, the code shows a "Processing" UI (a spinner or animation).

The Background Update: While the user is staring at the spinner, your Server Action finishes the AI call and updates the document in the database with the new Priority, Category, and changes the flag to 1.

The Instant Trigger: Because of the "Live Wire," Firestore pushes the new data to the browser the millisecond the database changes.

The UI Update: Your code sees the flag is now 1. It automatically hides the spinner and reveals the complaint details. The user feels like the app "figured it out" right in front of them.
